{"_id":"69e63a8d31e228f31bc923ec","roadmapSlug":"leetcode","nodeId":"P9U_DFbutAYwQGZjjf-oP","description":"# Rotate Image\n\nGiven an n by n matrix, rotate it 90 degrees clockwise in place. You first transpose the matrix (swap across the diagonal), then reverse each row. This problem teaches you that complex in-place transformations often decompose into two simpler operations applied in sequence.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Rotate Image","url":"https://leetcode.com/problems/rotate-image/","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7ab6"},{"type":"video","title":"Rotate Image (Leetcode 48) | Full solution","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ux058jpRB9Y","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7ab7"},{"type":"video","title":"Rotate Image - Leetcode 48 - Arrays & Strings (Python)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-jhbxNJijyE","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7ab8"}],"createdAt":"2026-04-20T14:39:09.601Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-22T09:44:44.827Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/leetcode/content/P9U_DFbutAYwQGZjjf-oP.md"}